# Code owners for the CHAP Model Marketplace.
#
# This file decides WHETHER a pull request needs maintainer review, by path.
# It cannot decide HOW MANY approvals are needed — GitHub's code-owner rule
# only ever means "at least one owner approved". The three-approval count in
# registry.yaml (`review_policy.required_approvals`) is enforced separately by
# .github/workflows/model-review-gate.yml, which reads its roster from the
# owner entries in this file. Keep the two in sync by editing only this file.
#
# Anything NOT listed here is deliberately unowned: site/ changes need no
# maintainer approval, only green CI. That is the fast path for frontend work.
#
# NOTE: GitHub silently ignores owners without write access to this
# repository. Until every handle below is a collaborator, the ruleset's
# "require review from Code Owners" rule stays OFF — see README.md.

# The registry itself: models, the index, and benchmark records.
/models/                    @edvinstava @mortenoh @knutdrand @Halvardgithub @ivargr
/registry.yaml              @edvinstava @mortenoh @knutdrand @Halvardgithub @ivargr
/benchmarks/                @edvinstava @mortenoh @knutdrand @Halvardgithub @ivargr

# The gate itself. Without this, a "frontend" PR could edit the rules that
# govern model review.
/.github/                   @edvinstava @mortenoh @knutdrand @Halvardgithub @ivargr

# Registry truth enforced in code: the schema every YAML file is validated
# against, and the flag that publishes benchmark views.
/site/src/lib/schema.ts     @edvinstava @mortenoh @knutdrand @Halvardgithub @ivargr
/site/src/lib/flags.ts      @edvinstava @mortenoh @knutdrand @Halvardgithub @ivargr
